+# Homepage performance monitoring
+
+`performance-monitor.js` observes browser-provided interaction contentful paint and
+soft-navigation entries. It does not change links or introduce client-side routing.
+
+Read the most recent 100 reports with
+`window.dailyGrindPerformance.getReports()`. Subscribe to
+`window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => { /* consume detail */ })`
+to connect your own analytics. No reports are sent over the network automatically.
+
+- `interaction-paint`: `duration` in milliseconds from the initiating input to
+  contentful paint presentation. Reports label navigation links, Order Now, and
+  Seasonal Favorites cards. Other interactions are labeled `other`.
+- `soft-navigation`: first contentful paint (`fcpDuration`) and latest largest
+  contentful paint (`lcpDuration`) in milliseconds relative to the initiating input.
+  Finalized on the next soft navigation, when hidden, or on pagehide. Correlation
+  uses interaction IDs and includes paints before the URL changes. Paths exclude
+  queries and fragments.
+
+Interaction reports are successive larger paint candidates, not a promise that
+every image, animation, or asynchronous task has finished. These browser APIs
+track contentful updates after an interaction, rather than only the next frame.
+Inputs without a contentful update may produce no report. Ordinary document
+navigations cannot measure destination rendering from the departing homepage;
+instrument destination pages separately for that purpose.
+
+Check `window.dailyGrindPerformance.supported` for feature availability. Unsupported
+browsers skip these observers without substituting approximate frame timings.
+When available, Event Timing supplies control labels; captured input timestamps
+also label short interactions. Buffered paints recorded before monitoring began
+may have no control label.
+
+Run automated checks with `node --test tests/performance-monitor.test.cjs`.
+These use mocked performance entries and do not launch a browser or server.
